{"Opa-janDani": [{"id": "Opa-janDani", "headword": "औप-जन्धनि", "headword_slp1": "Opa-janDani", "fold": "Opa-janDani", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vedic-index-macdonell-keith", "senses": [{"gloss": "Aupa-jandhani, ‘descendant of Upajandhana,’ is the patronymic of a teacher mentioned in the Bṛhadāraṇyaka upaniṣad as a pupil of āsuri, and also as a pupil of sāyakāyana.\nFoot notes ii. 6, 3; iv. 6, 3 (in Vaṃśas).\niv. 5, 27 (in the Mādhyaṃdina recension)", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["aupa", "aupa-jandhani", "aupajandhani", "jandhani", "औप", "औपजन्धनि", "जन्धनि", "ఔప", "ఔప-జన్ధని", "ఔపజన్ధని", "జన్ధని", "ಔಪ", "ಔಪ-ಜನ್ಧನಿ", "ಔಪಜನ್ಧನಿ", "ಜನ್ಧನಿ"], "synonyms_slp1": ["aupa", "aupa-jandhani", "aupajandhani", "jandhani", "Opa", "OpajanDani", "janDani", "ఔప", "ఔప-జన్ధని", "ఔపజన్ధని", "జన్ధని", "ಔಪ", "ಔಪ-ಜನ್ಧನಿ", "ಔಪಜನ್ಧನಿ", "ಜನ್ಧನಿ"]}], "Opa-tasvini": [{"id": "Opa-tasvini", "headword": "औप-तस्विनि", "headword_slp1": "Opa-tasvini", "fold": "Opa-tasvini", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vedic-index-macdonell-keith", "senses": [{"gloss": "Aupa-tasvini, ‘descendant of Upatasvina,’ is the patronymic of rāma in the Śatapatha brāhmaṇa (iv. 6, 1. 7).", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["aupa", "aupa-tasvini", "aupatasvini", "tasvini", "औप", "औपतस्विनि", "तस्विनि", "ఔప", "ఔప-తస్విని", "ఔపతస్విని", "తస్విని", "ಔಪ", "ಔಪ-ತಸ್ವಿನಿ", "ಔಪತಸ್ವಿನಿ", "ತಸ್ವಿನಿ"], "synonyms_slp1": ["aupa", "aupa-tasvini", "aupatasvini", "tasvini", "Opa", "Opatasvini", "tasvini", "ఔప", "ఔప-తస్విని", "ఔపతస్విని", "తస్విని", "ಔಪ", "ಔಪ-ತಸ್ವಿನಿ", "ಔಪತಸ್ವಿನಿ", "ತಸ್ವಿನಿ"]}], "Opa-manyava": [{"id": "Opa-manyava", "headword": "औप-मन्यव", "headword_slp1": "Opa-manyava", "fold": "Opa-manyava", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vedic-index-macdonell-keith", "senses": [{"gloss": "Aupa-manyava, ‘descendant of upamanyu,’ is the patronymic of various persons: see kāmboja, Prācīnaśāla, mahāśāla. The best known bearer of the name is the grammarian who disagreed with the onomatopetic theory of the